<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pushmataha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1764–<a href="/years/1824">1824</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pushmataha (c. 1764–1824) was a Choctaw chief, head of one of the three Choctaw districts. He rejected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tecumseh">Tecumseh</a>'s call for a pan-Indian alliance in 1811, led Choctaw warriors on the American side against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sticks">Red Sticks</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/creek-war">Creek War</a> and fought under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>. He negotiated treaties ceding land to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and died in Washington in 1824 during a treaty delegation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pushmataha.jpg" alt="Pushmataha" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Bird King · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pushmataha_high_resolution.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
